.md
## Animation loop & paddles
__Timecode: 1:27:19__
`Do`, `For`, and other loops with `Pause` block the kernel. Event-driven animation is preferable for continuous animations, game loops, etc.

__Timecode: 1:28:12__
For user input, we use `EventHandler` with the `"mousemove"` event to assign the mouse's y-coordinate to the paddle position.


%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Animation loop & paddles
__Timecode: 1:27:19__
`Do`, `For`, and other loops with `Pause` block the kernel. Event-driven animation is preferable for continuous animations, game loops, etc.

__Timecode: 1:28:12__
For user input, we use `EventHandler` with the `"mousemove"` event to assign the mouse's y-coordinate to the paddle position.


%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
paddles = {{-0.75,0.}, {0.75,0.}};
$paddles = 2{0.02, 0.21};

handler[_] := With[{},
  If[Abs[ball[[2,1]]] >= 1, 
    ball[[{1,2}, 1]] = ball[[{2,1}, 1]];
  ];

  If[Abs[ball[[2,2]]] >= 1, 
    ball[[{1,2}, 2]] = ball[[{2,1}, 2]];
  ];  
  
  ball = integrate[ball, {0.,0.}, 0.1];
  paddles = paddles;
];

EventHandler[Graphics[{
  Pink, Disk[ball[[2]] // Offload, Offset[{5,5}]],
  Black, 
  Translate[Rectangle[
    -$paddles/2,$paddles/2, RoundingRadius->0.02
  ], paddles[[1]]//Offload],
  Translate[Rectangle[
    -$paddles/2,$paddles/2, RoundingRadius->0.02
  ], paddles[[2]]//Offload],
  Dashed, Line[{{0.0, -0.75}, {0.0,0.75}}],
  
  EventHandler[
    AnimationFrameListener[ball//Offload],
    handler
  ]
}, AspectRatio->1, ImageSize->200, PlotRange->1], {
  "mousemove" -> Function[xy,
    paddles[[1,2]] = xy[[2]];
  ]
}]//Framed 

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md


![](/attachments/paddle1-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter-697.gif)


Here, `AnimationFrameListener` fires `handler` only __once before the window's paint cycle__ and is clamped by the window's refresh rate. For the next event, it must be *retriggered* by a change to the `ball` symbol. This ensures that the next paint event will not fire until `handler` has finished executing and useful data has arrived at the frontend.
To stop the animation — that is, to break the cycle — run:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%


![](/attachments/paddle1-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter-697.gif)


Here, `AnimationFrameListener` fires `handler` only __once before the window's paint cycle__ and is clamped by the window's refresh rate. For the next event, it must be *retriggered* by a change to the `ball` symbol. This ensures that the next paint event will not fire until `handler` has finished executing and useful data has arrived at the frontend.
To stop the animation — that is, to break the cycle — run:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
handler[_] := Null;

